      "message": "Hi Ben / Brian:\n\nThis is the follow-up to https://skia-review.googlesource.com/c/skia/+/545396.\n\nAs you may recall, in that CL we added SkSurfaceProps parameters to several public-facing APIs, but specifically omitted SkPictureShader APIs, in favor of propagating the props from the target surface.\n\nThat\u0027s this CL.\n\nIt\u0027s a bit involved, since there are so many levels/places where the props need to be passed/propagated.  Let me know if you know an easier way to accomplish any of this.\n\nThere are three tests that fail in Chromium with this enabled, so it\u0027s currently behind a build-flag for staging.  Chromium will only require minor changes.  You can follow along with my Chromium-side changes here:  https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/3759131.  \n\nI don\u0027t know if any other first-party Skia consumers (Android, etc.) will need similar staging.\n\nThanks!",
